1
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:13,577
Around our world.

2
00:01:13,660 --> 00:01:16,000
Stop me up!

3
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:27,560
Oh

4
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:00,591
What's the matter, Robin?

5
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:04,544
You have to tell me,
didn't my mom come by here?

6
00:02:05,420 --> 00:02:06,780
Now hold on a minute.

7
00:02:06,980 --> 00:02:08,197
Where did that come from?

8
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:11,221
Why would you think your
mother was back in Ohara?

9
00:02:11,480 --> 00:02:12,857
I've severed all bonds.

10
00:02:12,940 --> 00:02:16,822
No matter what, I can't let her
become the daughter of a criminal.

11
00:02:17,540 --> 00:02:19,893
I wish she was here, too, but she's not.

12
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:21,990
Oh, yeah!

13
00:02:22,073 --> 00:02:23,060
We're in trouble!

14
00:02:23,160 --> 00:02:26,037
I heard there are navy battleships
coming to the island right now!

15
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:28,377
They're trying to get rid of
all the scholars on Ohara!

16
00:02:28,460 --> 00:02:31,401
The people in town must
be stirring up bad rumors.

17
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:37,157
The truth is, that's no battleship, and
they won't be getting rid of anyone.

18
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:39,577
The government is paying
us a visit, though.

19
00:02:39,660 --> 00:02:42,857
And that means the library
will be under an investigation.

20
00:02:42,940 --> 00:02:43,770
A harsh one.

21
00:02:43,880 --> 00:02:44,880
So listen up.

22
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:47,417
No matter what those
government agents say or do,

23
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:49,337
you absolutely cannot let them know?

24
00:02:49,420 --> 00:02:51,637
that you're an archaeologist
like the rest of us.

25
00:02:51,720 --> 00:02:52,857
Since you're so young,

26
00:02:52,940 --> 00:02:55,637
as long as you keep quiet, no
one will think you're a scholar.

27
00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:56,602
You understand?

28
00:02:58,540 --> 00:02:59,370
Move it!

29
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:02,317
Stop what you're doing!

30
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:04,812
Put your hands in the air and go outside!

31
00:03:04,900 --> 00:03:07,117
Don't you think you're
being a bit violent?

32
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:09,317
The researchers here at
the Tree of Knowledge

33
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:11,157
are being charged with the heinous crime?

34
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:12,657
of deciphering poneglyphs.

35
00:03:12,740 --> 00:03:14,297
We'll be investigating the library,

36
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:16,737
so everyone get out of our
way and leave the building.

37
00:03:16,820 --> 00:03:18,997
You'd better treat this place with care.

38
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:23,097
The value of this collection is well
beyond your imagination, I assure you.

39
00:03:23,180 --> 00:03:25,377
I don't have to listen to a word you say.

40
00:03:25,460 --> 00:03:27,100
Take him outside! Yes, sir!

41
00:03:27,860 --> 00:03:29,566
Attention, citizens of Ohara!

42
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:32,297
I regret to inform you that
the scholars of this island

43
00:03:32,380 --> 00:03:37,000
may be devils in disguise plotting
to destroy the world. What? But why?

44
00:03:37,180 --> 00:03:39,497
Our scholars are the pride
of every person in Ohara.

45
00:03:39,580 --> 00:03:41,537
They would never dream of
doing something like that.

46
00:03:41,620 --> 00:03:42,977
From this point forward,

47
00:03:43,060 --> 00:03:46,037
we will be conducting a large-scale
search of the entire island.

48
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:46,997
During that time,

49
00:03:47,080 --> 00:03:49,877
all those who are not related to
the research center must take a form

50
00:03:49,960 --> 00:03:54,136
of identification and head to the
evacuation ship on the West Seashore.

51
00:03:54,300 --> 00:03:55,130
Evacuation?

52
00:03:55,213 --> 00:03:56,043
That's ridiculous!

53
00:03:56,126 --> 00:03:59,917
Even if the scholars did do something
wrong that still has nothing to do with us,

54
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,837
you can't kick us off our own island!

55
00:04:01,920 --> 00:04:05,155
Our only obligation was to
pass on this message to you.

56
00:04:06,180 --> 00:04:07,697
Disregard our warning if you like,

57
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:12,180
but we won't be held responsible,
should any unfortunate accidents occur.

58
00:04:18,520 --> 00:04:19,360
You heard him?

59
00:04:19,460 --> 00:04:20,290
Yeah, everyone!

60
00:04:20,373 --> 00:04:21,317
Back in the West Shore!

61
00:04:21,400 --> 00:04:23,929
I don't want to have
any part of this mess!

62
00:04:28,100 --> 00:04:29,020
I've been shot!

63
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:30,400
This is it for me!

64
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:32,700
I'm a gunner, dammit! A gunner!

65
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:33,997
Contact the higher-ups!

66
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:37,740
Tell them I want my son to take
over for me! Calm down, Chief.

67
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:38,730
Just take a look.

68
00:04:38,813 --> 00:04:41,077
The bullet went through
your sleeve, that's all.

69
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:42,220
Oh, I see.

70
00:04:45,320 --> 00:04:47,120
I'll aim to kill next time.

71
00:04:47,260 --> 00:04:49,260
Well, if it isn't Nico Olvia.

72
00:04:49,720 --> 00:04:53,097
I find it hard to believe that a
devious criminal like you would end

73
00:04:53,180 --> 00:04:56,697
up on this island completely by
coincidence after your daring escape.

74
00:04:56,780 --> 00:04:57,662
In other words,

75
00:04:57,840 --> 00:05:01,137
despite the fact that you've denied your
connection to the Scholars of O 'Hara,

76
00:05:01,220 --> 00:05:03,357
You've shown up at their doorstep just in

77
00:05:03,440 --> 00:05:05,777
time to warn them of our
little investigation.

78
00:05:05,860 --> 00:05:10,742
Now, in my humble opinion, that very clearly
labels them as your partners in crime.

79
00:05:10,940 --> 00:05:12,587
You've no idea why I'm here.

80
00:05:12,700 --> 00:05:14,818
That doesn't prove one single thing.

81
00:05:15,640 --> 00:05:18,817
I'm sure you've cooked up plenty
of excuses to cover for them.

82
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:20,841
You're a clever woman, after all.

83
00:05:21,060 --> 00:05:22,457
But that doesn't really matter,

84
00:05:22,540 --> 00:05:26,577
because we don't have to prove your
connection to the Ohara scholars anymore.

85
00:05:26,660 --> 00:05:29,477
Now that we're here, we can search
every little nook and cranny.

86
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:33,557
I doubt it'll take long before we find
evidence of their poneglyph research.

87
00:05:33,640 --> 00:05:37,757
The government's quite confident in
this, and you know they're never wrong.

88
00:05:37,840 --> 00:05:40,369
This has been in the
works for a long time.

89
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:45,317
Capturing you after six years of hide-and-seek
was nothing more than the final push.

90
00:05:45,400 --> 00:05:48,417
There are plenty of poneglyph
researchers around the world,

91
00:05:48,500 --> 00:05:50,257
and each time we captured one,

92
00:05:50,340 --> 00:05:53,693
we tried to find any connection
they might have to Ohara.

93
00:05:54,060 --> 00:05:55,589
Can you guess why that is?

94
00:05:56,580 --> 00:05:57,520
Don't tell me.

95
00:05:57,680 --> 00:05:59,504
You're making an example of us?

96
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:00,510
Exactly.

97
00:06:00,593 --> 00:06:03,240
If we crush this holy
ground of archaeology,

98
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:05,877
the entire academic
world will take notice.

99
00:06:05,960 --> 00:06:08,497
It's the perfect opportunity
to show the world exactly

100
00:06:08,580 --> 00:06:11,657
what happens to those who
research the blank century.

101
00:06:11,740 --> 00:06:16,034
Then, the battleships from headquarters
waiting on standby are here, too.

102
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:17,880
Well, look at that.

103
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:20,099
You are a clever woman, aren't you?

104
00:06:20,280 --> 00:06:25,045
Yes, as you might guess, there to ensure
that not even a single criminal escapes.

105
00:06:25,380 --> 00:06:29,300
However, as a matter of form, we
still need to verify their guilt.

106
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:31,260
We aren't pirates, after all.

107
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:34,837
So I came all this way to conduct
a compulsory investigation

108
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:38,096
of the island and chase off
anyone who's not involved.

109
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:40,597
It's curtains for you and your friends.

110
00:06:40,680 --> 00:06:41,880
There's no escape.

111
00:06:43,380 --> 00:06:44,600
Take her down.

112
00:06:56,400 --> 00:06:57,737
Hey, what are you doing?

113
00:06:57,820 --> 00:06:59,617
All the books here are world treasures.

114
00:06:59,700 --> 00:07:01,457
Take them outside and shut them up.

115
00:07:01,540 --> 00:07:03,480
Move it, you bastards.

116
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:06,017
They must have a secret
room somewhere around here.

117
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:07,806
Don't stop until you find it.

118
00:07:11,820 --> 00:07:13,740
This is worse than I thought.

119
00:07:14,700 --> 00:07:18,582
The battleships are here already
and there's a whole mess of them.

120
00:07:20,300 --> 00:07:21,712
That should be everyone.

121
00:07:22,220 --> 00:07:24,396
Good, now don't let them go anywhere.

122
00:07:25,580 --> 00:07:27,837
Look, they're rounding
up all the scholars.

123
00:07:27,920 --> 00:07:29,273
What did they do wrong?

124
00:07:29,380 --> 00:07:31,917
They say they were cooking up
a plan to destroy the world.

125
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:33,118
That can't be true.

126
00:07:33,580 --> 00:07:35,437
Where is the evacuation ship?

127
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:36,857
It's on the west seashore.

128
00:07:36,940 --> 00:07:37,770
Hurry!

129
00:07:37,853 --> 00:07:38,683
Everyone, run!

130
00:07:38,840 --> 00:07:40,487
Who knows what might happen?

131
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,737
Robin, they said there's
an evacuation ship waiting.

132
00:07:43,820 --> 00:07:46,577
We don't know what the government
is going to do anymore.

133
00:07:46,660 --> 00:07:49,220
You should get out while you can. No way!

134
00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:52,217
There's nothing but mean
people on that stupid boat.

135
00:07:52,300 --> 00:07:53,737
I'm staying here with my friends.

136
00:07:53,820 --> 00:07:54,650
Robin!

137
00:07:54,733 --> 00:07:55,797
I'm the same as you, aren't I?

138
00:07:55,880 --> 00:07:56,710
That's enough!

139
00:07:56,793 --> 00:07:57,623
Just go!

140
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:02,304
Looks like you have the
situation under control.

141
00:08:02,540 --> 00:08:04,128
Thank you very much, Chief!

142
00:08:04,680 --> 00:08:05,974
I was quite surprised.

143
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:10,376
Nobody warned me there were such
ferocious beasts wandering the island.

144
00:08:13,880 --> 00:08:16,260
But it makes for a fine trophy, huh?

145
00:08:18,540 --> 00:08:19,370
Olivia?

146
00:08:20,520 --> 00:08:22,167
All right, listen carefully.

147
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:24,560
This woman is an escaped prisoner.

148
00:08:24,760 --> 00:08:26,777
We executed her comrades
after we found out

149
00:08:26,860 --> 00:08:29,037
that they'd been
deciphering ancient texts.

150
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:32,137
But we still have a couple
of matters left to clear up.

151
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:33,680
So let me be frank here.

152
00:08:33,980 --> 00:08:35,274
If she's your partner,

153
00:08:35,380 --> 00:08:39,498
just come out with it already so I
can get this over with and go home.

154
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:43,020
How awful of them to
hurt someone like that.

155
00:08:43,260 --> 00:08:46,300
Robin, for the last time, go! Hurry!

156
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:47,990
Robin?

157
00:08:56,920 --> 00:08:59,020
Robin, my little girl,

158
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:06,120
you've grown so much.

159
00:09:07,560 --> 00:09:08,390
Olvia.

160
00:09:12,980 --> 00:09:14,560
What are they doing?

161
00:09:14,740 --> 00:09:17,097
If they're not careful, they're
going to burn the whole tree down.

162
00:09:17,180 --> 00:09:19,417
I never thought they would
take such drastic measures.

163
00:09:19,500 --> 00:09:22,100
Wow, they aren't holding back, are they?

164
00:09:25,560 --> 00:09:27,031
Hello, is this the chief?

165
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:28,280
Yeah, it's me.

166
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:30,037
We found a hidden room in the basement.

167
00:09:30,120 --> 00:09:32,737
They have a huge tablet
there, probably a poneglyph,

168
00:09:32,820 --> 00:09:36,517
and a massive collection of research
documents discussing the ancient texts.

169
00:09:36,600 --> 00:09:37,600
Nice work.

170
00:09:38,720 --> 00:09:39,550
Clerk.

171
00:09:41,940 --> 00:09:43,820
Well, scholars of Ohara,

172
00:09:44,420 --> 00:09:47,820
I'm afraid your death sentence
has already been decided.

173
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:49,460
It's a pity.

174
00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:55,180
I hate to lose so many fine scholars,
but you're really forcing my hand here

175
00:10:00,740 --> 00:10:02,040
Wow, what a letdown.

176
00:10:02,280 --> 00:10:04,357
I came all this way just to say that?

177
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:07,337
Guess we'd better report
to the five elder stars.

178
00:10:07,420 --> 00:10:08,250
Roger

179
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:11,657
Professor, they aren't
really going to kill you?

180
00:10:11,740 --> 00:10:15,377
They wouldn't do that to someone for
just learning about history, would they?

181
00:10:15,460 --> 00:10:17,137
Stupid brat, what do you know?

182
00:10:17,220 --> 00:10:19,397
They may say they're
learning about history,

183
00:10:19,480 --> 00:10:21,157
but the truth is they're
learning how to revive

184
00:10:21,240 --> 00:10:23,657
an ancient weapon so they
can commit mass murder.

185
00:10:23,740 --> 00:10:24,570
You're wrong!

186
00:10:24,653 --> 00:10:26,737
They would never do anything like that!

187
00:10:26,820 --> 00:10:27,996
Don't bother, Robin.

188
00:10:28,100 --> 00:10:31,117
It's pointless to discuss the
matter with an errand boy like him.

189
00:10:31,200 --> 00:10:32,030
What's that?

190
00:10:32,113 --> 00:10:35,737
Is it really the ancient weapon itself
that the world government is afraid of?

191
00:10:35,820 --> 00:10:36,650
Professor!

192
00:10:36,733 --> 00:10:37,563
Be careful!

193
00:10:37,646 --> 00:10:41,320
They're on the line now,
Chief. Good. Hold on! Eh?

194
00:10:41,720 --> 00:10:46,117
Before you put all of us to death, allow
me to speak to the five Elder Stars.

195
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:48,317
Although we still have much to learn,

196
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:51,197
we have proudly continued
our research for many years.

197
00:10:51,280 --> 00:10:52,497
So at the very least,

198
00:10:52,580 --> 00:10:56,757
I would like to share our hypothesis on
the blank century with the world's leaders.

199
00:10:56,840 --> 00:11:00,000
Heh, stubborn old fart. Hey! Yes, sir?

200
00:11:00,160 --> 00:11:02,572
I'm begging you, please, get out of here!

201
00:11:02,680 --> 00:11:06,033
If you hear what I have to
say, you'll become a criminal!

202
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:07,630
Professor!

203
00:11:08,280 --> 00:11:11,437
Hey, it looks like they found the
people from the library guilty.

204
00:11:11,520 --> 00:11:12,797
You gotta be kidding me!

205
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:13,710
Bad news!

206
00:11:13,793 --> 00:11:16,877
There's a bunch of Navy battleships
closing in on the island from the east.

207
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:18,437
This is about to get real ugly.

208
00:11:18,520 --> 00:11:19,873
We better evacuate now.

209
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:21,940
What is that?

210
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:23,420
It's a giant.

211
00:11:27,300 --> 00:11:29,140
Where are you, Robin?

212
00:11:30,020 --> 00:11:33,255
You've got to get off this
island before it's too late.

213
00:11:38,720 --> 00:11:41,337
Have they made the order
for the Buster Call yet?

214
00:11:41,420 --> 00:11:42,900
We're still on standby.

215
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:45,790
Hurry!

216
00:11:45,873 --> 00:11:47,640
Run to the evacuation ship!

217
00:11:51,260 --> 00:11:53,200
So this is a poneglyph, huh?

218
00:11:53,840 --> 00:11:54,670
Yeah,

219
00:11:54,753 --> 00:11:56,157
I heard even if we shoot it with a cannon,

220
00:11:56,240 --> 00:11:58,277
it won't leave a single
scratch on the thing.

221
00:11:58,360 --> 00:12:01,797
I can't believe these creepy things
are hidden all over the world.

222
00:12:01,880 --> 00:12:03,020
I don't like it.

223
00:12:03,720 --> 00:12:05,020
Is that so?

224
00:12:05,380 --> 00:12:07,440
Yes, the evidence is clear.

225
00:12:07,820 --> 00:12:10,317
This calls for nothing
short of the death penalty.

226
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:12,037
We're waiting for your order.

227
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:13,160
It's unfortunate.

228
00:12:13,820 --> 00:12:18,077
Seeing as they've broken the law so
blatantly, there's really no other option.

229
00:12:18,160 --> 00:12:20,260
We must enforce our own rules.

230
00:12:20,660 --> 00:12:23,366
We don't need your mock
sympathy, Elder Stars.

231
00:12:23,500 --> 00:12:24,500
Save your breath.

232
00:12:25,160 --> 00:12:28,257
You're talking to the leaders
of the world, you damn criminal.

233
00:12:28,340 --> 00:12:29,399
Show some respect.

234
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:34,040
That must be Professor Clover, Ohara's
foremost authority on archaeology.

235
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:36,020
I'm familiar with your work.

236
00:12:36,200 --> 00:12:39,417
You've contributed much to
the world's cultural heritage.

237
00:12:39,500 --> 00:12:42,037
It's sad to see a man of
your intellect go astray.

238
00:12:42,120 --> 00:12:45,238
The history of this planet
belongs to all of mankind.

239
00:12:45,860 --> 00:12:48,140
No matter what that history may be,

240
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:51,097
you don't have the right to
forbid us from learning it.

241
00:12:51,180 --> 00:12:53,440
No one does. Professor.

242
00:12:53,620 --> 00:12:55,377
If one can read the poneglyphs,

243
00:12:55,460 --> 00:12:57,817
then it's also possible
that they can revive the

244
00:12:57,900 --> 00:13:00,777
ancient weapons and place
the world in serious peril.

245
00:13:00,860 --> 00:13:03,213
Even if you have the best of intentions,

246
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:06,908
someone else could come along
and use your research for evil.

247
00:13:07,160 --> 00:13:08,760
Be it good or bad,

248
00:13:09,140 --> 00:13:13,440
mankind has the responsibility to
accept whatever their history may hold.

249
00:13:13,620 --> 00:13:15,997
As long as we don't succumb
to fear and ignorance,

250
00:13:16,080 --> 00:13:18,577
we will be prepared for
anything that may come.

251
00:13:18,660 --> 00:13:20,440
That's idealistic. Is it?

252
00:13:20,580 --> 00:13:24,240
Or are you just making convenient
excuses to suit your needs?

253
00:13:25,220 --> 00:13:28,500
In truth, there are two
mysteries left unsolved.

254
00:13:28,700 --> 00:13:30,877
Of course we want to read the Poneglyph,

255
00:13:30,960 --> 00:13:35,297
but the reason why they were made in
the first place is interesting as well.

256
00:13:35,380 --> 00:13:38,197
Why was their message so important
that they had to inscribe

257
00:13:38,280 --> 00:13:41,633
it on unbreakable stone to
pass on to future generations?

258
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:44,897
Why were they hidden and
scattered across the world?

259
00:13:44,980 --> 00:13:47,215
Why were they not stored in a library?

260
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:51,297
The only logical conclusion is
that they feared their message

261
00:13:51,380 --> 00:13:54,797
would be too easily destroyed
if they had written it on paper.

262
00:13:54,880 --> 00:13:57,180
In other words, they had an enemy.

263
00:13:57,560 --> 00:14:01,384
Someone who was afraid of the
information they wanted to pass on.

264
00:14:02,780 --> 00:14:05,880
What are you trying to
imply, Professor Clover?

265
00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:07,997
Since the ancients have disappeared,

266
00:14:08,080 --> 00:14:12,786
we must assume that they were defeated
by this enemy And that whoever they were,

267
00:14:12,880 --> 00:14:14,586
they survived through history

268
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:22,217
It may be no coincidence that roughly 800
years in the past When the blank century

269
00:14:22,300 --> 00:14:27,340
came to an end The organization we now
call the World Government was founded

270
00:14:30,600 --> 00:14:35,197
therefore if this unknown enemy was indeed
the world government it might be in their

271
00:14:35,280 --> 00:14:39,757
best interest to erase this inconvenient
piece of information and let the ancients

272
00:14:39,840 --> 00:14:42,317
disappear into a fabricated blank century

273
00:14:42,400 --> 00:14:45,037
by analyzing ancient
manuscripts and piecing

274
00:14:45,120 --> 00:14:47,297
together what we could
from the few pornoglyphs

275
00:14:47,380 --> 00:14:49,537
we were able to find we discovered the

276
00:14:49,620 --> 00:14:54,417
existence of a previously unknown country
although the details we found were a bit

277
00:14:54,500 --> 00:14:57,057
scarce we believe it
was a grand and powerful

278
00:14:57,140 --> 00:15:00,177
kingdom and yet despite their strength not

279
00:15:00,260 --> 00:15:03,037
a trace remains or
rather those traces were

280
00:15:03,120 --> 00:15:05,457
deliberately erased but they were prepared

281
00:15:05,540 --> 00:15:10,537
for this possibility even as they faced
the threat of extinction and so they etched

282
00:15:10,620 --> 00:15:12,897
their history in stone
before their kingdom

283
00:15:12,980 --> 00:15:14,777
was crushed under the might of the allied

284
00:15:14,860 --> 00:15:19,277
nations now known as the world government
thus the reason why the poneglyphs were

285
00:15:19,360 --> 00:15:23,637
made becomes quite clear i see that's a

286
00:15:23,720 --> 00:15:26,377
bold hypothesis it's true that the ancient

287
00:15:26,460 --> 00:15:29,117
weapons would be a threat to the world but

288
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:31,417
more so than weapons
what i believe the world

289
00:15:31,500 --> 00:15:33,637
government is afraid of is the history

290
00:15:33,720 --> 00:15:36,377
surrounding this lost
kingdom its existence and

291
00:15:36,460 --> 00:15:38,677
its ideologies are so
dangerous to you that

292
00:15:38,760 --> 00:15:41,757
you would kill to keep
them secret although

293
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:45,617
we still don't know what makes you fear
this kingdom we do at least know its name

294
00:15:45,700 --> 00:15:48,137
since we've gone so far already perhaps

295
00:15:48,220 --> 00:15:50,985
Perhaps you'd like me to
share it with you now.

296
00:15:52,320 --> 00:15:53,480
Kill him!

297
00:16:03,960 --> 00:16:04,790
Professor!

298
00:16:08,780 --> 00:16:10,940
You left us no choice.

299
00:16:15,220 --> 00:16:17,540
How dare you! No! Professor!

300
00:16:18,320 --> 00:16:20,260
Ohara knows too much.

301
00:16:22,720 --> 00:16:24,880
You may give the order to attack.

302
00:16:25,180 --> 00:16:27,360
Or don't move an inch! No!

303
00:16:27,820 --> 00:16:29,700
You mustn't let anyone escape!

304
00:16:37,060 --> 00:16:42,497
Now then, with a golden transponder snail
entrusted to me by Admiral Sengoku...

305
00:16:42,580 --> 00:16:43,410
Professor!

306
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:44,790
Robin!

307
00:16:45,300 --> 00:16:46,460
You fool!

308
00:16:46,700 --> 00:16:48,780
I told you to run! Hurry!

309
00:16:49,040 --> 00:16:50,880
I invoked the Buster Call!

310
00:16:51,700 --> 00:16:53,160
And that's a wrap.

311
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:55,415
He pressed something!

312
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:56,460
What is that?

313
00:16:57,760 --> 00:16:59,640
Get out of here! Go!

314
00:17:00,280 --> 00:17:01,110
No!

315
00:17:01,193 --> 00:17:02,591
I don't want to be alone!

316
00:17:02,680 --> 00:17:04,680
You have to stop being so selfish!

317
00:17:04,900 --> 00:17:06,300
This isn't the time!

318
00:17:07,980 --> 00:17:08,810
Robin!

319
00:17:12,420 --> 00:17:14,100
It's the Buster Call!

320
00:17:14,680 --> 00:17:16,517
All battleships to your positions!

321
00:17:16,600 --> 00:17:17,835
Prepare to open fire!

322
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:21,230
What?

323
00:17:21,800 --> 00:17:22,840
Hey, look!

324
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:26,280
The Tree of Knowledge is on fire!

325
00:17:26,760 --> 00:17:28,348
Dammit, what are you doing?

326
00:17:28,480 --> 00:17:29,362
Are you insane?

327
00:17:29,580 --> 00:17:31,600
Isn't it enough to take our lives?

328
00:17:32,700 --> 00:17:34,180
Hey, it's not my fault.

329
00:17:34,460 --> 00:17:37,989
Must have caught fire when they
bombed your secret basement.

330
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:40,460
Stop this! Right now!

331
00:17:40,700 --> 00:17:42,717
You can't replace the documents in there!

332
00:17:42,800 --> 00:17:43,757
Don't you realize that?

333
00:17:43,840 --> 00:17:44,722
You don't move!

334
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:46,190
Whoa.

335
00:17:46,273 --> 00:17:47,448
We don't need guns anymore.

336
00:17:48,340 --> 00:17:50,869
Time for the government
agents to pull out.

337
00:17:52,180 --> 00:17:53,720
Protect the books.

338
00:17:55,640 --> 00:17:57,620
Let's put out the fire. Hurry!

339
00:18:08,140 --> 00:18:09,820
Pass the water over here.

340
00:18:11,680 --> 00:18:14,460
Carry as many books outside as you can.

341
00:18:28,340 --> 00:18:30,097
Bring that woman with you.

342
00:18:30,180 --> 00:18:32,157
Get up.

343
00:18:32,240 --> 00:18:36,217
There's still some info we
have to ring out of her!

344
00:18:36,300 --> 00:18:37,417
She can't die yet.

345
00:18:37,500 --> 00:18:39,853
Just make sure she doesn't escape again.

346
00:18:44,940 --> 00:18:45,770
Mommy!

347
00:18:50,020 --> 00:18:52,620
Please, Robin, run while you still can.

348
00:18:53,120 --> 00:18:54,820
You can't die here.

349
00:18:55,160 --> 00:18:56,300
Not like this.

350
00:18:57,320 --> 00:18:58,150
Mommy, no!

351
00:19:01,960 --> 00:19:02,790
Go!

352
00:19:03,100 --> 00:19:04,380
We're done for.

353
00:19:04,680 --> 00:19:06,327
There's no point in staying.

354
00:19:10,060 --> 00:19:10,890
Robin!

355
00:19:11,040 --> 00:19:12,140
Robin, don't!

356
00:19:20,160 --> 00:19:22,780
You're my mother, aren't you?

357
00:19:27,900 --> 00:19:29,600
Make up your mind, Olvia.

358
00:19:29,880 --> 00:19:32,233
Are you going to board this ship or not?

359
00:19:33,540 --> 00:19:34,800
I'm holding her back.

360
00:19:34,960 --> 00:19:36,320
Just hurry and get on.

361
00:19:37,380 --> 00:19:38,210
Molly!

362
00:19:38,720 --> 00:19:39,550
Molly!

363
00:19:39,633 --> 00:19:40,463
Molly!

364
00:19:41,620 --> 00:19:42,797
I'm sorry, Robin.

365
00:19:42,880 --> 00:19:45,780
I can never call myself your mother again.

366
00:19:46,480 --> 00:19:51,520
After all these years, after all I've
done, I don't have the right anymore.

367
00:20:00,900 --> 00:20:01,730
Monster!

368
00:20:02,040 --> 00:20:02,870
Monster!

369
00:20:03,100 --> 00:20:05,560
She's so scary, her mom ran away!

370
00:20:06,040 --> 00:20:08,497
Hey, that's my daughter's
dress, you take it off!

371
00:20:08,580 --> 00:20:11,077
I'm sorry Aunt Roji, I
just wanted to try it on!

372
00:20:11,160 --> 00:20:13,600
You sure eat a lot for a freeloader.

373
00:20:22,220 --> 00:20:24,000
Please answer me!

374
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:28,020
Are you my mom?

375
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:35,400
Hold on.

376
00:20:35,640 --> 00:20:37,522
That girl your daughter or what?

377
00:20:39,360 --> 00:20:40,190
No.

378
00:20:41,220 --> 00:20:46,177
Oh yeah I'm sorry little girl you

379
00:20:46,260 --> 00:20:49,637
must be confusing me with someone else

380
00:20:49,720 --> 00:20:55,217
even if it comes to this I don't want
you to be the daughter of a criminal.

381
00:20:55,300 --> 00:21:01,120
Oh yeah huh what a weird
little brat right let's go!

382
00:21:16,200 --> 00:21:18,300
It's me! It's Robin!

383
00:21:18,800 --> 00:21:22,920
I've grown since the last time,
so maybe you don't recognize me.

384
00:21:23,380 --> 00:21:25,851
I've been waiting for you all these years.

385
00:21:26,260 --> 00:21:27,380
Are you sure?

386
00:21:27,980 --> 00:21:28,837
Are you sure?

387
00:21:28,920 --> 00:21:30,780
You're really...

388
00:21:31,900 --> 00:21:33,460
Not my mom!

389
00:21:35,320 --> 00:21:37,300
Just once, someday,

390
00:21:37,740 --> 00:21:42,440
I wanted to hold your hand and
walk together like a family.

391
00:21:43,560 --> 00:21:48,160
I studied hard to become an archaeologist
so I could go to sea with you.

392
00:21:48,500 --> 00:21:50,360
I can read the Poneglyphs too.

393
00:21:52,160 --> 00:21:53,600
What did she say?

394
00:21:53,920 --> 00:21:55,260
Robin, no!

395
00:21:56,020 --> 00:21:58,140
So please, look at me.

396
00:21:58,540 --> 00:22:00,480
Let me stay with you.

397
00:22:01,220 --> 00:22:02,050
Mom!

398
00:22:02,880 --> 00:22:03,710
Robin.

399
00:22:05,600 --> 00:22:07,537
I've waited so long.

400
00:22:07,620 --> 00:22:09,760
We're finally together.

401
00:22:10,340 --> 00:22:12,320
Don't leave me alone again.

402
00:22:18,540 --> 00:22:19,540
Oh, no!

403
00:22:19,780 --> 00:22:20,956
Now what's going on?

404
00:22:21,200 --> 00:22:23,620
Now commencing the Buster Call.

405
00:22:23,900 --> 00:22:25,780
All ships fire at once.

406
00:22:25,960 --> 00:22:28,837
Everything on the island
of Ohara is your target.

407
00:22:28,920 --> 00:22:30,038
Let nothing remain.

408
00:22:30,320 --> 00:22:34,496
The research conducted here was far
more extensive than we anticipated.

409
00:22:34,700 --> 00:22:37,017
Make sure that knowledge is not passed on.

410
00:22:37,100 --> 00:22:39,218
Do not allow it to leave the island.

411
00:22:39,840 --> 00:22:41,664
Annihilate the devils of Ohara.

412
00:22:42,140 --> 00:22:43,434
Turn it to the ground.

413
00:22:43,520 --> 00:22:45,040
In the name of justice!

414
00:22:49,500 --> 00:22:51,380
Damn it! What the hell?

415
00:22:52,100 --> 00:22:53,817
Can't you wait till we leave the island?

416
00:22:53,900 --> 00:22:56,000
You're gonna kill us! Stop it!

417
00:22:57,440 --> 00:22:59,852
The three of knowledge took a direct hit!

418
00:23:00,020 --> 00:23:02,537
They're using their
highest power against us.

419
00:23:02,620 --> 00:23:06,337
They staged their investigation, but
they were planning this from the start.

420
00:23:06,420 --> 00:23:07,250
Bastards.

421
00:23:07,333 --> 00:23:10,317
Hey, Chief, that girl said
she can read the Poneglyphs.

422
00:23:10,400 --> 00:23:12,140
Yeah, she did, didn't she?

423
00:23:12,380 --> 00:23:14,017
I don't know if it's true or not, though.

424
00:23:14,100 --> 00:23:16,537
Probably safer to wipe
her out, just in case.

425
00:23:16,620 --> 00:23:17,917
Don't let her leave the island.

426
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:19,720
Remember her face, all right?

427
00:23:20,060 --> 00:23:21,160
We're retreating.

428
00:23:21,380 --> 00:23:22,615
Then I'll grab Olvia.

429
00:23:24,420 --> 00:23:25,250
Screw it!

430
00:23:25,340 --> 00:23:26,777
The situation has changed!

431
00:23:26,860 --> 00:23:27,690
Just run!

432
00:23:27,773 --> 00:23:30,397
I'm not gonna get blown up trying
to follow some stupid order!

433
00:23:30,480 --> 00:23:33,068
Our number one priority
is keeping me alive!

434
00:23:33,920 --> 00:23:34,750
Retreat!

435
00:23:34,833 --> 00:23:35,929
Everyone back to the ship!

436
00:23:44,040 --> 00:23:46,864
Put out the fire on that
side before it spreads!

437
00:23:46,960 --> 00:23:49,080
Protect the library at all costs!

438
00:24:09,460 --> 00:24:12,080
I've been waiting a long time to do this.

439
00:24:14,920 --> 00:24:15,960
I'm glad.

440
00:24:20,060 --> 00:24:20,890
Robin!

441
00:24:24,320 --> 00:24:25,150
Mommy!

442
00:24:28,580 --> 00:24:30,240
Robin, forgive me.

443
00:24:30,760 --> 00:24:31,590
Please.

444
00:24:31,940 --> 00:24:35,380
This is my fault for not
watching over you with more care.

445
00:24:36,220 --> 00:24:39,279
Is it really true that you
can read the pornoglyphs?

446
00:24:40,300 --> 00:24:44,340
I had to learn, since I
wanted to be a scholar.

447
00:24:44,540 --> 00:24:46,877
I never knew my little
girl was an archaeologist.

448
00:24:46,960 --> 00:24:47,842
That's amazing.

449
00:24:48,160 --> 00:24:51,042
You must have studied hard
while I was gone, huh?

450
00:24:51,540 --> 00:24:54,128
These aren't things
that just anyone can do.

451
00:24:54,300 --> 00:24:55,540
I'm so proud.

452
00:25:02,500 --> 00:25:03,330
Fortunately,

453
00:25:03,413 --> 00:25:06,817
the only ones who know about this are
the officials who were here earlier.

454
00:25:06,900 --> 00:25:09,194
We can't afford to waste any more time.

455
00:25:09,620 --> 00:25:11,640
Alpha, take Robin and run!

456
00:25:11,980 --> 00:25:14,437
If you can sneak her
onto the evacuation ship,

457
00:25:14,520 --> 00:25:17,108
she might still be able
to leave the island.

458
00:25:20,180 --> 00:25:21,010
Robin!

459
00:25:21,200 --> 00:25:24,357
I've been looking all
over for you. It's Saul.

460
00:25:24,440 --> 00:25:26,675
So you met with your mother after all.

461
00:25:26,800 --> 00:25:29,640
Sol, why in the world are you here?

462
00:25:29,820 --> 00:25:31,160
Guess it must be fate.

463
00:25:31,420 --> 00:25:35,657
I just happened to wash up here and your
little girl was the one who found me.

464
00:25:35,740 --> 00:25:38,097
Anyhow, we ain't got
time to chat right now.

465
00:25:38,180 --> 00:25:39,945
You gotta get off this island.

466
00:25:40,500 --> 00:25:45,380
I'll be fine, but I need you to take
care of Robin for me, please. But why?

467
00:25:45,560 --> 00:25:46,442
What about you?

468
00:25:46,640 --> 00:25:48,405
Are you going to come with me?

469
00:25:49,340 --> 00:25:50,580
Olivia, are you?

470
00:25:50,760 --> 00:25:51,819
I can't leave yet.

471
00:25:52,180 --> 00:25:53,886
There's something left to do.

472
00:25:54,160 --> 00:25:54,990
No, Mom!

473
00:25:55,120 --> 00:25:56,473
You can't leave me now!

474
00:25:56,560 --> 00:25:57,677
I'll stay here with you!

475
00:25:57,760 --> 00:26:00,460
I don't want to lose you again! Robin,

476
00:26:00,700 --> 00:26:02,406
if you're a scholar of Ohara,

477
00:26:02,540 --> 00:26:05,237
you should know that history
is mankind's greatest treasure.

478
00:26:05,320 --> 00:26:09,297
Now that it's been passed on, it will
illuminate the path to your future.

479
00:26:09,380 --> 00:26:11,920
However, you must pass it on as well,

480
00:26:12,320 --> 00:26:15,438
or its light will disappear
with the next generation.

481
00:26:15,680 --> 00:26:16,820
Share those books!

482
00:26:17,040 --> 00:26:17,870
I won't take these!

483
00:26:17,953 --> 00:26:20,700
We weren't trying to
uncover some dark secret,

484
00:26:21,020 --> 00:26:24,844
we simply wanted to hear the voices
of the past and protect them.

485
00:26:25,120 --> 00:26:25,950
Unfortunately,

486
00:26:26,040 --> 00:26:30,880
our research ends here, but time
marches on, even if Ohara is destroyed.

487
00:26:32,000 --> 00:26:34,353
And as surely as we believe in the past,

488
00:26:34,540 --> 00:26:37,305
we believe in the future
that you will inherit.

489
00:26:38,140 --> 00:26:39,460
What does that mean?

490
00:26:42,220 --> 00:26:43,660
Someday, you'll know.

491
00:26:46,680 --> 00:26:47,510
Hurry.

492
00:26:48,020 --> 00:26:49,920
Take her and go, Saul!

493
00:26:51,660 --> 00:26:53,120
Are you sure?

494
00:26:53,740 --> 00:26:54,570
Yeah

495
00:26:54,920 --> 00:26:55,917
Stop it!

496
00:26:56,000 --> 00:26:58,640
I want to stay with you! Mommy! No!

497
00:27:01,160 --> 00:27:03,920
I was happy to hear
you call me that again.

498
00:27:05,040 --> 00:27:06,037
Thank you.

499
00:27:06,120 --> 00:27:07,697
From now on.

500
00:27:07,780 --> 00:27:09,277
For my sake as well?

501
00:27:09,360 --> 00:27:11,600
You must live, Robin!

502
00:27:30,260 --> 00:27:32,880
Vice Admiral Kuzan! What now?

503
00:27:33,220 --> 00:27:34,157
It looks like...

504
00:27:34,240 --> 00:27:35,780
No, wait, it's gotta be!

505
00:27:35,920 --> 00:27:37,717
So are you gonna tell me or not?

506
00:27:37,800 --> 00:27:39,300
Spit it out already, man!

507
00:27:39,500 --> 00:27:40,457
It's the deserter!

508
00:27:40,540 --> 00:27:41,677
Vice Admiral Saul!

509
00:27:41,760 --> 00:27:43,000
Please don't!

510
00:27:43,100 --> 00:27:45,357
You have to take me back! I can't!

511
00:27:45,440 --> 00:27:46,322
There's no way!

512
00:27:46,920 --> 00:27:49,060
Don't cry, Robin! Be proud!

513
00:27:49,280 --> 00:27:51,060
Your mama's a wonderful woman!

514
00:27:51,480 --> 00:27:53,009
Ohara's a wonderful place!

515
00:27:53,700 --> 00:27:54,997
You gotta remember that!

516
00:27:55,080 --> 00:27:57,139
It's up to you to pass it on, okay?

517
00:27:57,300 --> 00:28:00,660
Ohara was so brave, they
fought against the whole world!

518
00:28:04,320 --> 00:28:05,957
Are you crazy?!

519
00:28:06,040 --> 00:28:07,511
Capturing them is enough!

520
00:28:07,760 --> 00:28:09,657
They ain't even pirates, they're scholars!

521
00:28:09,740 --> 00:28:13,137
Are you so weak you can't reel
them in without blowing them up?

522
00:28:13,220 --> 00:28:16,700
We shoot down these researcher
ships one after another,

523
00:28:17,020 --> 00:28:20,608
but I still can't find any sense
in killing these poor folks.

524
00:28:20,920 --> 00:28:23,300
Vice Admiral Saul, we found a survivor!

525
00:28:24,560 --> 00:28:26,580
You're nothing but murderers!

526
00:28:27,620 --> 00:28:28,740
You're scholars.

527
00:28:29,080 --> 00:28:30,597
Why do you need ancient weapons?

528
00:28:30,680 --> 00:28:32,033
You don't know a thing.

529
00:28:32,140 --> 00:28:34,377
You don't even know why you're killing us!

530
00:28:34,460 --> 00:28:36,117
That's a Vice Admiral you're speaking to!

531
00:28:36,200 --> 00:28:37,297
The weapons are just an excuse.

532
00:28:37,380 --> 00:28:40,857
Why don't you try thinking about
what you're doing for once?

533
00:28:40,940 --> 00:28:44,293
You're just afraid of a past
that you know nothing about!

534
00:28:45,900 --> 00:28:47,700
This is a top-secret mission.

535
00:28:47,880 --> 00:28:49,160
The Buster Call.

536
00:28:49,780 --> 00:28:53,957
It's an Alto attack in which five
vice-admills command ten battleships.

537
00:28:54,040 --> 00:28:55,417
I want you to take part.

538
00:28:55,500 --> 00:28:56,917
They're just scholars, right?

539
00:28:57,000 --> 00:28:58,647
Why do we have to go so far?

540
00:28:59,040 --> 00:29:02,657
Even the ones we've captured before
don't seem like they care about weapons.

541
00:29:02,740 --> 00:29:04,477
They just want to learn
more about history.

542
00:29:04,560 --> 00:29:09,097
If their research is so dangerous, why
don't we help them so nothing goes wrong?

543
00:29:09,180 --> 00:29:12,137
Least you can do is give me some
proof that these folks are bad.

544
00:29:12,220 --> 00:29:15,037
Because to me, it seems like
we're the criminals here.

545
00:29:15,120 --> 00:29:17,057
Are you questioning the government?

546
00:29:17,140 --> 00:29:18,552
Just follow your orders.

547
00:29:22,860 --> 00:29:24,742
I've got some questions for you.

548
00:29:25,920 --> 00:29:27,220
You think we can talk?

549
00:29:27,400 --> 00:29:28,635
This is an emergency!

550
00:29:28,800 --> 00:29:32,017
Black Admiral Saul has taken
the prisoner and deserted!

551
00:29:32,100 --> 00:29:33,077
This won't do.

552
00:29:33,160 --> 00:29:36,740
He knows too much about our
next operation. After them.

553
00:29:37,120 --> 00:29:38,960
Shots all will be at any cost.

554
00:29:39,320 --> 00:29:40,673
Open fire if necessary.

555
00:29:41,360 --> 00:29:44,817
Truth will be showing up any minute
now, but I'll take care of them.

556
00:29:44,900 --> 00:29:47,957
You know, you won't be able to
return to the Navy after this.

557
00:29:48,040 --> 00:29:48,900
Fine by me.

558
00:29:49,160 --> 00:29:52,637
Now that I got this doubt in my heart,
ain't no point in staying anyway.

559
00:29:52,720 --> 00:29:57,077
I know the law is the law, but the way
they're acting this time is downright cruel.

560
00:29:57,160 --> 00:29:59,572
So I'm following my own sense of justice.

561
00:29:59,760 --> 00:30:01,777
Now you get to that island
and warn your friends.

562
00:30:01,860 --> 00:30:03,800
I'm not going to thank you.

563
00:30:03,920 --> 00:30:06,000
Well, good luck to you either way.

564
00:30:09,780 --> 00:30:10,610
Fire!

565
00:30:13,280 --> 00:30:16,398
We're not targeting the
idol, we're not targeting me!

566
00:30:22,980 --> 00:30:24,820
It hit him! I'm sorry!

567
00:30:25,620 --> 00:30:26,450
Don't apologize!

568
00:30:26,533 --> 00:30:28,217
He's the criminal's accomplice now!

569
00:30:28,300 --> 00:30:29,897
My apologies, Robin.

570
00:30:29,980 --> 00:30:32,080
that must have scared you.

571
00:30:33,680 --> 00:30:35,040
Wait here a sec.

572
00:30:35,740 --> 00:30:37,660
Are you the one firing at us?

573
00:30:37,840 --> 00:30:41,260
What if you'd hurt that poor
little girl, you damn fools?

574
00:30:41,700 --> 00:30:43,320
Vice Admiral, please stop!

575
00:30:43,580 --> 00:30:48,600
I don't know about justice anymore,
but I do know I can protect my friend!

576
00:30:49,080 --> 00:30:50,220
Stop it, Saul!

577
00:30:50,640 --> 00:30:51,800
You're scaring me!

578
00:30:52,060 --> 00:30:53,140
Hope you're ready,

579
00:30:53,400 --> 00:30:57,880
because if you make an enemy out of
me, there's gonna be hell to play!

580
00:31:10,840 --> 00:31:15,177
I want to tell you

581
00:31:15,260 --> 00:31:18,220
what I want to say.

582
00:31:19,000 --> 00:31:19,830
I can't tell you

583
00:31:19,913 --> 00:31:23,417
what I

584
00:31:23,500 --> 00:31:29,840
want to say.

585
00:31:31,040 --> 00:31:34,480
Now, the light of a single one.

586
00:31:36,840 --> 00:31:37,937
I feel that I've found.

587
00:31:38,020 --> 00:31:42,780
If I can follow it,

588
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:46,537
I'll run away from the future!

589
00:31:46,620 --> 00:31:49,120
I won't stay.

590
00:31:53,400 --> 00:31:55,380
Once again, once again.
